s in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T21:33:24-07:00","id":1083336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083334#post1083334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Archery one was done in 2e, and it was Thrown. You could reverse engineer it pretty easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I put it in Archery based on Vance's comment on the developer thread (that it would probably be Archery based on the media it's portrayed in).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T22:44:43-07:00","id":1083344,"title":"","content":"Athletics-Something, anything with swimming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T22:52:39-07:00","id":1083351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support#post1083309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Larceny: Disguise others on par with Solar disguise-self Charms</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this needs to exist. Disguise Charms are about more than convincing make-up and costume, they're about <i>selling </i>that disguise and making people believe it is real. Just because a Solar can do that amazingly well doesn't mean he can make others do it just as well. That would imply that Solars can make non-Solars just as awesome as Solars. That doesn't make any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T23:27:32-07:00","id":1083362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083344#post1083344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Athletics-Something, anything with swimming.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were some of these in earlier drafts but they ended up being removed. It makes sense to remove them and I understood what they were doing, because Swimming Charms are weird.<br /> <br /> If the Swimming Charms aren't connected to the rest of Athletics at all, you end up with a bunch of charms that feel disconnected from others; in addition, these charms additionally have limited scope; each thing you make require a swimming charm is something a normal character can't do; sometimes it wouldn't matter, other times it could matter a good deal; imagine if something like being able to swim in armor was a charm; then now every Exalt must have a charm to help them swim in armor, in addition to everything else it says about the setting. These weird, unconnected charms then begin to make setting statements and require other Exalts and godly beings to conform to those situations in a way that may not be effective.<br /> <br /> If they are connected to the other charms, it becomes more akin to requiring you to take Sail Charms to ride your Horse. If you, for instance, are required to take a Swimming Charm to get access to something like Triumph-Forged God-Body, and your game takes place in a place where you are unlikely to end up having a knock down, drag out fight in the middle of a lake or ocean (Not really impossible, all things considered), then you're essentially implementing a tax on TFGB in this example where it has a larger cost then noted because you have to buy charms you might not ever get to use, or only get to use once or twice. Compare that to charms for running fast or lifting something, which are generally much more universally applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:04:56-07:00","id":1083525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083362#post1083362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were some of these in earlier drafts but they ended up being removed. It makes sense to remove them and I understood what they were doing, because Swimming Charms are weird.<br /> <br /> If the Swimming Charms aren't connected to the rest of Athletics at all, you end up with a bunch of charms that feel disconnected from others; in addition, these charms additionally have limited scope; each thing you make require a swimming charm is something a normal character can't do; sometimes it wouldn't matter, other times it could matter a good deal; imagine if something like being able to swim in armor was a charm; then now every Exalt must have a charm to help them swim in armor, in addition to everything else it says about the setting. These weird, unconnected charms then begin to make setting statements and require other Exalts and godly beings to conform to those situations in a way that may not be effective.<br /> <br /> If they are connected to the other charms, it becomes more akin to requiring you to take Sail Charms to ride your Horse. If you, for instance, are required to take a Swimming Charm to get access to something like Triumph-Forged God-Body, and your game takes place in a place where you are unlikely to end up having a knock down, drag out fight in the middle of a lake or ocean (Not really impossible, all things considered), then you're essentially implementing a tax on TFGB in this example where it has a larger cost then noted because you have to buy charms you might not ever get to use, or only get to use once or twice. Compare that to charms for running fast or lifting something, which are generally much more universally applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with this though is then it ends looking like Swimming is the one thing Exalted can't do better then mortals.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we already have (or should have at least):<br /> <br /> - Lunars who can grow gills or change into some sort of marine life.<br /> <br /> - Water Aspect DB who can breath and move freely underwater.<br /> <br /> If other exalts can't get swimming charms then these two might as well be only ones who can ever journey underwater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:18:26-07:00","id":1083530,"title":"","content":"How are the existing set of Solar Athletics (and Resistance) Charms inapplicable to swimming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:22:46-07:00","id":1083534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083530#post1083530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are the existing set of Solar Athletics (and Resistance) Charms inapplicable to swimming?</div> </div> </div> </div>this is the better solution tbh.<br /> <br /> Why should a Rush be different because you're swimming versus running. Just Lightning Speed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:27:05-07:00","id":1083536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083534#post1083534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this is the better solution tbh.<br /> <br /> Why should a Rush be different because you're swimming versus running. Just Lightning Speed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. <br /> <br /> Lightning Speed is applicable when the Solar uses flying Charms, right? Also when climbing or swinging from tree branches and vines?<br /> <br /> Why would swimming be excluded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:43:44-07:00","id":1083543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083536#post1083536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly.<br /> <br /> Lightning Speed is applicable when the Solar uses flying Charms, right? Also when climbing or swinging from tree branches and vines?<br /> <br /> Why would swimming be excluded?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For <i>my </i>purposes, this want emerged after we realized how hard it is for a Solar to do something like, say, survey a sunken ship.<br /> Granted, this is an intreasting weak spot (like stealths weakness to dogs) that might be intentional. Obviously strength/speed charms are good for that, but I meant more 'holding my breath underwater' and 'navigating underwater' charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:54:08-07:00","id":1083550,"title":"","content":"I'd echo what Flare said, but I do think there's some room. A charm that goes &quot;you can move as easily as underwater as on land&quot; is probably all you'd need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:08:24-07:00","id":1083555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, this is an intreasting weak spot <b>(like stealths weakness to dogs)</b> that might be intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can buy Mental Invisibility Technique, or Sound and Scent Banishing Attitude -<i> a Stealth Charm that makes you not produce scent </i>- what more do you need?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I meant more 'holding my breath underwater'</div> </div> </div> </div>You can already do that with Sail and Survival. I don't see much necessity in extending it beyond that natively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and 'navigating underwater' charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on what you mean by &quot;navigating,&quot; that's either Awareness, Sail, or Survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-25-2017, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:20:23-07:00","id":1083638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083555#post1083555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can buy Mental Invisibility Technique, or Sound and Scent Banishing Attitude -<i> a Stealth Charm that makes you not produce scent </i>- what more do you need?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly hadn't dug super deep into Stealth. I kinda preffered that weakeness as a cool bit of trivia, ah well. Guess that's gone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083555#post1083555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can already do that with Sail and Survival. I don't see much necessity in extending it beyond that natively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double checking Sail, because I'm almost certain you can't with Survival...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083555#post1083555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on what you mean by &quot;navigating,&quot; that's either Awareness, Sail, or Survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Traversing' would have been better. Apparently I should look at Sail? Didn't remember that from when I looked earlier.<br /> <br /> Honestly, its a 1 charm thing that I would add. Something that let you operate underwater for longer and longer amounts of time or the like based on Stamina. Something to expand on the Iron Lungs merit, more than anything. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:35:33-07:00","id":1083655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083351#post1083351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this needs to exist. Disguise Charms are about more than convincing make-up and costume, they're about <i>selling </i>that disguise and making people believe it is real. Just because a Solar can do that amazingly well doesn't mean he can make others do it just as well. That would imply that Solars can make non-Solars just as awesome as Solars. That doesn't make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't have to be on the same level, but I really think &quot;make people think my cow is a lion!&quot; should be in the range of Solar Larceny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:45:40-07:00","id":1083661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083638#post1083638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly hadn't dug super deep into Stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're talking about gaps in the Solar Charmset without having read the Solar Charmset?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083638#post1083638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double checking Sail, because I'm almost certain you can't with Survival...</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Fathoms Blessed, while it doesn't enhance how long you can hold your breath, prevents you from drowning when your breath runs out; Element-Resisting Prana lets you &quot;walk underwater with no ill effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083638#post1083638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Traversing' would have been better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still don't see how swimming-specific Athletics Charms would factor into it. If you're having trouble getting around underwater because water's hard to see through, that's Awareness. If you're having trouble finding your way around underwater, Salty Dog Method. If the pressures of the ocean's depths are getting to you, Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit and/or Element-Resisting Prana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083638#post1083638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently I should look at Sail?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should if you want to complain about competency holes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083638#post1083638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't remember that from when I looked earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Salty Dog Method allows you to navigate to anywhere you've been.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083638#post1083638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, its a 1 charm thing that I would add. Something that let you operate underwater for longer and longer amounts of time or the like based on Stamina. Something to expand on the Iron Lungs merit, more than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to put it in your game, but please don't mind me not doing the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-25-2017, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:59:58-07:00","id":1083670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083661#post1083661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you're talking about gaps in the Solar Charmset without having read the Solar Charmset?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the whole thing, don't have it in perfect memory except for specific charms I've used as a player or players use. However, thank you for correcting me on what I thought was missing! My comment was off the top of my head and not cross checked. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083661#post1083661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Fathoms Blessed, while it doesn't enhance how long you can hold your breath, prevents you from drowning when your breath runs out; Element-Resisting Prana lets you &quot;walk underwater with no ill effects.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not recalled Element Resisting Prana as doing that, and didn't remember that Sail charm. Thank you very much for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083661#post1083661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should if you want to complain about competency holes..</div> </div> </div> </div>A hole that apparently didn't exist. Again, sorry if I gave offense, I posted with double checking all the charms in the core. I will keep that in mind in the future. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:03:32-07:00","id":1083674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083670#post1083670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the whole thing, don't have it in perfect memory except for specific charms I've used as a player or players use. However, thank you for correcting me on what I thought was missing! My comment was off the top of my head and not cross checked.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I often make the mistake of assuming my memory is trustworthy, myself. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> \u200bThe way you'd said it, though, about having not dug that deep, I had thought you meant you'd only actually read the first couple of Charms or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083670#post1083670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had not recalled Element Resisting Prana as doing that, and didn't remember that Sail charm. Thank you very much for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it's less that it can't be done and more that only certain kinds of characters get to do it natively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083670#post1083670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, sorry if I gave offense...</div> </div> </div> </div>We're good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-25-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:28:25-07:00","id":1084320,"title":"","content":"As far as swimming goes...I wrote these a while back. I don't think they're necessarily very good, but I felt like swimming needed <i>something</i> and I assumed that swimming a range band is at least a little more difficult than walking one (if you disagree it's an easy fix though).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The following Charms are subject to the caveat that we don't really have much in the way of basic rules for swimming. My default assumption is that a character stuck in the water is normally going to be making Athletics rolls to do much of anything besides tread water, since that's about what I'd go with if I were Storytelling.<br /> <br /> Nimble Minnow Prana<br /> Cost: 1m (+1m); Mins: Athletics 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One turn<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> Quickened by Essence, the Solar slides through the water with effortless ease. For the rest of the turn, the Exalt can move in water as easily as on land; for example, she may use her movement action to swim one range band (horizontally or vertically) without making a roll, and may likewise rush, disengage, take cover (if possible) or withdraw as though on land. The Solar may even leap out of the water as though jumping from a standing start. Additionally, the Exalt suffers no penalties to her Defense for being in or under the water. This Charm conveys no special ability to either breathe underwater or to see through the water, nor does it make difficult terrain (such as choppy waters or coral reefs) any less so.<br /> <br /> For an additional mote, the Solar's offensive actions are likewise unimpeded; she can swing a sword or even fire an arrow underwater.<br /> <br /> A Solar with Athletics 4+, Essence 2+ may instead commit six motes to increase the duration of this Charm to indefinite; this includes the ability to attack freely in the water.<br /> <br /> For the avoidance of doubt, Charms such as Lightning Speed work as well for a Solar using Nimble Minnow Prana as they would on land.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seal-Breath Technique<br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Resistance 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> Taking a deep, Essence-suffused breath, the Exalt learns to get the most out of every lungful of air. The Exalt multiplies the timeframe (normally (Stamina) minutes out of combat, or (Stamina x 2) turns in combat; see Exalted Third Edition, p. 232) for which he can survive without air by (Essence + 1).<br /> <br /> A repurchase at Resistance 4+, Essence 3+ instead costs five motes, and doubles the previous duration. The Exalt may also reflexively spend a point of Willpower when his time is up to respire pure Essence, effectively taking a new breath without need for air.<br /> <br /> <br /> Leaping Salmon Surge<br /> Cost: --; Mins: Athletics 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Nimble Minnow Prana<br /> <br /> Even a humble fish can swim against the rapids; it should come as no surprise that a Lawgiver could even swim up a waterfall with grace and ease. When maneuvering in or under water, the cost of the Athletics Excellency is permanently reduced to one mote per two dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lurking Undertow Method<br /> Cost: 2m (+3m); Mins: Brawl 4, Athletics 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Vicious Lunge, Nimble Minnow Prana<br /> <br /> Like a swift current, the Solar sweeps her unsuspecting victim away and under, exploiting all possible advantages. This Charm supplements a grapple gambit launched while both the Solar and her target are in water; if the gambit succeeds, the Solar's control roll is bolstered by double 9s if any of the following conditions are met, double 8s if any two of the conditions are met, and double 7s if at least three are met:<br /> <br /> - The Solar can move freely in water (as with Nimble Minnow Prana) and the victim cannot.<br /> - The Solar can see clearly underwater (as with Keen Sight Technique) and the victim cannot.<br /> - The Solar's attack was unexpected.<br /> - The victim cannot swim at all.<br /> <br /> In general, any character without at least Athletics 2+, or Athletics 1 with a specialty in swimming, cannot swim; it is up to the Storyteller if a more athletic character may also be unfamiliar with the water.<br /> <br /> At Brawl 5, Essence 3+, the Solar may spend an additional three motes upon succeeding at the control roll in order to reflexively drag her victim one range band downward before choosing which grapple effect to apply. (This occurs only on the turn the grapple is initiated, and not subsequent turns.) </div> </div> </div>I think the leaked playtest had a swimming Charm that basically made swimming as easy as walking without spending any motes; if you prefer, you could go with that and have Nimble Minnow Prana just cost a mote for doing something implausible like firing arrows from underwater.<br /> <br /> And yeah I'm not at all sure Lurking Undertow Method is balanced, especially the E3+ upgrade -- I just thought it was a cool effect for a swimming grappler to be able to take full advantage of.<br /> <br /> ...and I hadn't even thought of Element-Resisting Prana as a way to breathe underwater. Still, I feel like Resistance should at least potentially have a &quot;hold breath for a long time&quot; Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:51:55-07:00","id":1084334,"title":"","content":"Shooting an arrow out of the air with another arrow, I'm not sure that's in the charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T22:56:16-07:00","id":1084350,"title":"","content":"Why would it be? It would be a stunted Parry (with extremely high Difficulty, I'd expect). Ranged attacks can be parried, can't they? I don't have convenient access to the PDF at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:06:53-07:00","id":1084354,"title":"","content":"Non-Ninja Thrown charms are my biggest grip when it comes to holes in charm-sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:13:42-07:00","id":1084355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1084354#post1084354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Ninja Thrown charms are my biggest grip when it comes to holes in charm-sets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you explain what kind of &quot;non-ninja&quot; effects you're looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:44:45-07:00","id":1084360,"title":"","content":"Only a few of the Sail charms easily work with airships without some serious storyteller caveats, so I'd like to see more airship centric Sail charms for Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:54:22-07:00","id":1084363,"title":"","content":"Some love for Slow and Flame tagged archery would be nice; even just a care package to remind that not every solar uses bows for archery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T00:34:31-07:00","id":1084368,"title":"","content":"Well, this is something my brother and I have talked about things 3E Solar charms could do but don't yet. Some things we thought of:<br /> <br /> Archery: A charm for more reliably shooting inanimate and/or tiny targets.<br /> <br /> Craft: Charms to better craft with whatever materials you have at hand, beginning with ignoring penalties for using insufficient quantities of materials or inferior materials like green wood, and ending with being able to make armor from leaf litter or cake from sand.<br /> <br /> Integrity: A charm to channel the mundane talents of a friend on whose behalf you act kind of like Divine Mantle channels spirit charms.<br /> <br /> Lore: A charm to ensure your students can eventually reach the four dot level of whatever you teach them. A charm to learn a new ability related to your area of expertise as quickly as if you had a good teacher by deducing everything such a teacher could tell you.<br /> <br /> Peformance: A charm to integrate performance perfectly into other tasks, so that for example your motion in battle is also a deeply moving dance. (Although going by past editions this could be more a Dragon-Blooded thing?)<br /> <br /> Socialize: Something based around recognizing reincarnated souls and drawing from past-life social experience. A charm with Integrity charm prerequisites for quickly creating and adopting a persona in response to an attempt at mind-control.<br /> <br /> Thrown: A charm for manipulating things at a distance with thrown objects; e.g. throwing a key such that it unlocks a door or a pen such that it writes a letter (there was a charm like this in DotFA).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T01:03:57-07:00","id":1084377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1084355#post1084355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Could you explain what kind of &quot;non-ninja&quot; effects you're looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very few of the Thrown charms are actually any use for making an attack using thrown do more damage against a target. They have an alpha strike move and a bunch of &quot;This person can't make sound&quot; or &quot;People think the attack came from over there&quot; sort of effects, and while I have no problem with such at one point I tried to play a character that was thrown primary, but not particularly into hiding or misdirection and found there wasn't much that was at all useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:19:19-07:00","id":1084447,"title":"","content":"A lot of the crazy stuff could just be considered to be difficulty 10 tasks (shooting an arrow to deflect another arrow while blindfolded, throwing a key so it twists just right to open a lock with your teeth while hanging upside down, running across a field of grass without disturbing a single leaf while wearing clown shoes, etc). While they are highly improbable, they are not impossible, and they can be done with just high dice pools, supported by Excellency Charms and Probability Charms (reroll 10s, double 9s, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:20:17-07:00","id":1084471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083661#post1083661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Fathoms Blessed, while it doesn't enhance how long you can hold your breath, prevents you from drowning when your breath runs out; Element-Resisting Prana lets you &quot;walk underwater with no ill effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still don't see how swimming-specific Athletics Charms would factor into it. If you're having trouble getting around underwater because water's hard to see through, that's Awareness. If you're having trouble finding your way around underwater, Salty Dog Method. If the pressures of the ocean's depths are getting to you, Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit and/or Element-Resisting Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure Element-Resisting Prana doesn't let you breath underwater (IIRC there was a dev comment on this at some point?) and only protects from stuff like water pressure.<br /> <br /> I think there is room for an entry-level Athletics Charm that lets you hold your breath for some ungodly length of time (e.g. Stamina x Athletics hours). Black Fathoms Blessed isn't quite the same thing and also is very deep in the Sail tree, requiring 10 Charms and Essence 3.<br /> <br /> (Also Black Fathoms Blessed doesn't <i>really</i> work for this, since you still get incapacitated from drowning, you just don't die - so you are alive but unconscious at the bottom of the ocean, which is... not great.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","user":"AtG","date":". 04-27-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:27:18-07:00","id":1084473,"title":"","content":"I don't have my book on me - I assume there isn't anything helpful toward that end one integrity's meditation branch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:39:55-07:00","id":1084476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1084334#post1084334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shooting an arrow out of the air with another arrow, I'm not sure that's in the charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this as basically a reflexive clash, which Archery has (although it's extremely situational).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:37:01-07:00","id":1084498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1084471#post1084471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(IIRC there was a dev comment on this at some point?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I could find, not on these forums. The only mention made of E-RP by any of the writing/dev team <i>here </i>was Vance, and that was quite some time ago.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo be fair, I haven't checked RPG.net, but I'm pretty confident it's not over at GiantITP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:16:22-07:00","id":1084511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1084498#post1084498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I could find, not on these forums. The only mention made of E-RP by any of the writing/dev team <i>here </i>was Vance, and that was quite some time ago.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo be fair, I haven't checked RPG.net, but I'm pretty confident it's not over at GiantITP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, you're right. I would tend not to read it as granting water-breathing, both because I would read only the environmental damage reduction as an actual mechanical effect and because I don't feel water-breathing quite fits with the theme of Survival and the Charm. Cinematically, we see heroes manage to persevere through blizzards and hurricanes and firestorms and such, but it would be downright jarring to see one able to hold his breath indefinitely. And if you did see someone depicted as holding their breath for a incredible length of time, it would probably look more like a feat of athletic prowess. (Whereas unable to hold your breath, but able to survive drowning and be resuscitated definitely fits more in Sail.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:37:11-07:00","id":1084561,"title":"","content":"I would question the very premise of this thread: why do you need Charm support for everything?<br /> <br /> It's actually an interesting trend I've noticed. In my experience, at least, in practically every other RPG I've played, people have no trouble making rolls for just about anything that they want to do. Unskilled, low skill, completely outside their character's wheelhouse, doesn't matter. Pretty much every time I've played Exalted, though, if a character didn't have 5/5 ability/skill pool and generally at least three Charms for a skill, they would move heaven and earth to make sure they never had to make a particular roll.<br /> <br /> It's weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T14:44:32-07:00","id":1084706,"title":"","content":"There is very little support for throwing large things accurately, as an attack, or attacking with large objects. The closest I got with a very thorough reading of the rules was that you treat it as a large mundane improvised weapon. That seems very under-powered for what kinds of objects you can swing around at the highest ends of the Athletics tree.<br /> <br /> Most of the Thrown charms seem to be written with the idea that if you are throwing, you are probably a ninja, or a nimble circus performer. I would like some Thrown charms focused of the application of throwing things forcefully, or throwing larger weapons. I made a spear chucking Sol clone, four arms the whole shtick, and the charms as written were a little weird when used with a 10 foot long 6 inch diameter golden rod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5016-mobiushero","name":"MobiusHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5016_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T16:04:24-07:00","id":1084742,"title":"","content":"One doesn't have to be crazy to consider drowning an &quot;ill effect&quot; of being underwater, and thus be protected from it by the Charm.<br /> <br /> But I think this is a good one for Ask the Devs, and get a RAI for this old grouch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T07:49:23-07:00","id":1085024,"title":"","content":"Welp, I am wrong by WOG: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1084875#post1084875\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...75#post1084875</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T08:34:43-07:00","id":1085049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1085024#post1085024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, I am wrong by WOG: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1084875#post1084875\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...75#post1084875</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for sharing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:36:23-07:00","id":1085219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1083655#post1083655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be on the same level, but I really think &amp;quot;make people think my cow is a lion!&amp;quot; should be in the range of Solar Larceny.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound awesome. <br /> <br /> But as a Storyteller I cringe to think about the sort of shenanigans my players would get up to once they realized that was possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T22:22:27-07:00","id":1085368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpanishInquisition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1085219#post1085219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does sound awesome. <br /> <br /> But as a Storyteller I cringe to think about the sort of shenanigans my players would get up to once they realized that was possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shenanigans inappropriate for Solar con-artistry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T12:29:24-07:00","id":1085529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1083309-solar-feats-still-needing-charm-support?p=1084561#post1084561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would question the very premise of this thread: why do you need Charm support for everything?<br /> <br /> It's actually an interesting trend I've noticed. In my experience, at least, in practically every other RPG I've played, people have no trouble making rolls for just about anything that they want to do. Unskilled, low skill, completely outside their character's wheelhouse, doesn't matter. Pretty much every time I've played Exalted, though, if a character didn't have 5/5 ability/skill pool and generally at least three Charms for a skill, they would move heaven and earth to make sure they never had to make a particular roll.<br /> <br /> It's weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coik did you post in the wrong thread? This post seems to have nothing to do with the topic.<br /> <br /> Just in case though, to answer your question; while the topic indicates it being the case similar to your post, the actual discussion is very different. This topic is about feats that are relatively to overtly supernatural and thus require charms because they are beyond the scope of mortals in some ways.<br /> <br /> Regardless of my opinion on it, for instance, you can't make a boat fly as a mortal. If A Solar wants to do that, they need a charm.<br /> <br /> A more specific thing that I agree with is Glamourweaver's example of disguising a Cow as a Lion.<br /> <br /> Here is a picture of a dog disguised as a Lion;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2014/09/26/1411718051285_Image_galleryImage_Lion_Dog.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> That is not a Lion. It is a dog, but it definitely looks like a Lion at first glance. You may even think it is for a moment before you notice the difference in the muzzle, the movements of the tail, even the fact the Dog may be much smaller then a Lion. A mortal could probably disguise a Dog as a Lion for at least a little while, until you got close enough to it to see these differences. Or when it barks at you.<br /> <br /> Disguising a Cow as a Lion would be slightly harder; a Cow has hoofs, if it's a female cow it has udders, if it's a male cow it has horns. It's tail is constantly moving and shifting, more then other animals, and it might be covered in spots; Cows are also, as far as I know, usually not the same shade as Lions; they're black and white, I've seen the most, though some can be a pale beige appropriate to a lion. a Cow's face is longer, the way their face is set up is very different. If the cow decides to Moo, that would make it very obvious.<br /> <br /> It would be very hard for a mortal to disguise a Cow as a Lion. I would not make it impossible, but it would be far more difficult, and it would not work for an extended period of time; you would get a small shock value of a giant Lion, and that may confuse or unnerve people enough to change their perceptions, but if they stay close to the Cow they would eventually realize 'wait this isn't a Lion at all'. The reason I wouldn't make it impossible is because you are correct about one thing; in 2E, a very common late-game Charm to be created in the game in 2E was 'this feat you thought you could do without a charm? No, it requires this new, specific charm', which did create 'no one wants to do this without 3 charms of back-up', because often you couldn't do it at all without that charm. Thus, I wouldn't make the feat impossible, but I wouldn't let it stretch the bounds of realism to do things that are nigh-impossible; your cow-lion might scare off a random mook when they see it but the guild prince would take a good look at it and realize you don't actually have a Lion; not impossible, but it's going to fall apart under close scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Regardless, say that someone wants to consistently disguise animals as things that they are not, and often does this to ones that are not exactly the same. In such a case, I would make them a charm. They can buy it or not. Not 'Disguise Cow as Lion' charm, but rather a charm to allow you to do something like letting you disguise things as something it would be harder to do so. This wouldn't make the Cow not a Cow; It would still act like a Cow and the players would then be forced to either smooth talk the things it does that are too cow-like, or preemptively train it to act like a Lion; thus the charm is useful for people who wish to do this all the time, but it is not a one charm solution to the problem and doesn't always mean succes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T15:31:29-07:00","id":1085608,"title":"","content":"Yeah, running with the cow as lion example, I was thinking it could cover sound (so people mistake moos for roars), but not behavior. Everyone gets another awareness or investigation roll when the lion ignores red meat and starts grazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}